Z||000017||theogre||06-04-2001||07:34 PM||||Up to this post.... the page load is slower than plain pages but not like the older version. That one would hold up loading quite some time.<P>At this point you might want to play with the timing a bit if you keep it. With ani gif you can set both interframe timing and by setting the time on the last frame you can set how fast it repeats. Slowing an anigif down will make it less annoying in most cases. Slowing the repeat rate down is almost always good.<P>Just for the record... The old one played ok for me once it finally loaded. It just took a heck of a long time to load.<P>The problem isn't just your anigif... It's the whole bunch of sig images that appear on a given page. It doesn't take very many to really bloat up a page, animated or not. If there are a bunch of big ones, they can drag a page to it's knees.||||reg||1
